{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794994449,"nonce":"waFVyUxxXNsMxr4KZcxOUZWKfuo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABgUrfWg","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/205","origin":"github"},"title":"dd: couple(...).solve(tol=) always runs to max_iter when the subdomains use different discretisations","message":"With two different discretisations in the overlap (FEM and finite differences), `couple([...]).solve(tol=...)` always runs to `max_iter`. The loop has long converged; the stop test just cannot be met. Nothing reports that the tolerance was not reached.\n\nReproduced on release 0.4.2 and on `main` (b3dcdd22).\n\n## Cause\n\nThe plain forward loop (`_schwarz_forward_eager` in `jno/dd.py`) stops on the overlap jump, the largest difference between the two subdomain solutions in the overlap:\n\n```python\njump = float(jnp.max(jnp.abs(u0[ovj] - u1[ovj]))) if overlap.any() else 0.0\nif jump \u003c tol:\n    break\n```\n\nTwo different methods differ in the overlap by their discretisation error, at any number of sweeps. The jump therefore settles at a value set by the mesh size, far above the default `tol=1e-7`.\n\nThe differentiable path (`_schwarz_custom_root`) uses the change of the iterate between two sweeps, `max|U_new - U|`, which does go to zero. The two paths of the same solve stop on different quantities.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n`-div(k grad u) = f` on the unit square with a coefficient jump at `x = 0.5`, FEM on `x \u003c= 0.7`, finite differences on `x \u003e= 0.6`, exact solution known.\n\n```python\nimport jax\njax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\nimport numpy as np\nfrom shapely.geometry import box\n\nimport jno\nimport jno.jnp_ops as jnn\nfrom jno.dd import couple\n\nK_LEFT, K_RIGHT, FEM_END = 1.0, 10.0, 0.7\nconductivity = lambda x, m: m.where(x \u003c 0.5, K_LEFT, K_RIGHT)\nexact = lambda x, y, m: m.sin(np.pi * y) * ((x - 0.5) / conductivity(x, m) + m.cos(2 * np.pi * (x - 0.5)))\n\n\ndef source(x, y, m):\n    k = conductivity(x, m)\n    phi = (x - 0.5) / k + m.cos(2 * np.pi * (x - 0.5))\n    return -k * (-4 * np.pi**2 * m.cos(2 * np.pi * (x - 0.5)) - np.pi**2 * phi) * m.sin(np.pi * y)\n\n\ndef run(h, fdm_start, sweeps):\n    d = jno.domain(box(0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0))\n    d.region(\"soft\", box(0.0, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0))\n    d.region(\"stiff\", box(0.5, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0))\n    d.build_mesh(mesh_size=h)\n    pts = np.asarray(d.mesh_connectivity[\"points\"])[:, :2]\n    u_exact = exact(pts[:, 0], pts[:, 1], np)\n    xi, yi, _ = d.variable(\"interior\", split=True)\n    xb, yb, _ = d.variable(\"boundary\", split=True)\n    f, g = source(xi, yi, jnn), exact(xb, yb, jnn)\n    uf, vf = d.fem_symbols()\n    ui, vi = uf.bind(x=xi, y=yi), vf.bind(x=xi, y=yi)\n    fem = jno.fem([conductivity(xi, jnn) * (ui.x * vi.x + ui.y * vi.y) - f * vi, uf(xb, yb) - g])\n    u = d.unknown()\n    us = u.bind(x=xi, y=yi)\n    fdm = jno.fdm([-K_RIGHT * (us.d2(xi) + us.d2(yi)) - f, u(xb, yb) - g])\n    left, right = jno.shape.rect(0.0, 0.0, FEM_END, 1.0), jno.shape.rect(fdm_start, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0)\n    sol, info = couple([(fem, left), (fdm, right)]).solve(tol=1e-9, max_iter=sweeps, return_info=True)\n    err = np.linalg.norm(np.asarray(sol).reshape(-1) - u_exact) / np.linalg.norm(u_exact)\n    return err, info\n\n\nfor h in (0.1, 0.05, 0.025):\n    for sweeps in (40, 400):\n        err, info = run(h, 0.6, sweeps)\n        print(f\"h = {h}  max_iter = {sweeps}: error {err:.3e}  iterations {info['iterations']}  overlap jump {info['overlap_jump']:.3e}\")\n```\n\n| Mesh size | `max_iter` | Iterations used | Overlap jump | Error against the exact solution |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.1 | 40 | 40 | 2.559e-03 | 9.146e-03 |\n| 0.1 | 400 | 400 | 2.559e-03 | 9.146e-03 |\n| 0.05 | 40 | 40 | 4.274e-04 | 1.955e-03 |\n| 0.05 | 400 | 400 | 4.274e-04 | 1.955e-03 |\n| 0.025 | 40 | 40 | 1.129e-04 | 3.592e-04 |\n| 0.025 | 400 | 400 | 1.129e-04 | 3.592e-04 |\n\nThe solution is the same after 40 and after 400 sweeps, so the extra sweeps are wasted. With the default `max_iter=400` such a solve runs at least ten times the sweeps it needs.\n\n## Fix\n\nStop the plain loop on the change of the iterate between sweeps, as the differentiable path does, and keep the overlap jump as a reported quantity. If `max_iter` is reached without meeting `tol`, say so.","files":null}]}